    "muon": {
      "note": "Measured Muon optimizer rows, one entry for the whole campaign. `muon:` is the shipped multi-launch path (39 launches per shape group at the shipped ns_steps of 5) and `muon_fused:` is the fused path over the same buffers; a reader compares them row by row, and that pair is the promotion decision. The `ns=0` rows are the control: no Polar Express GEMM runs there, so their gap is the cost of one block size for sixteen phases and not of the fused arithmetic. The fused path is selected for no shape at these revisions (`kMuonFusedMaxElements` is 0), so `muon:` is the current default. Ranges are the spread across repeated runs. `phase0` and `phase1` are the two measurement gates the fusion had to clear before the fused step was written and promoted: the share of the step that is launch plus elementwise work, and the hand GEMM against cuBLAS. docs/kernels.md Part 1 sections 3 and 6 are the design and the gates; docs/performance.md section 2.1 is the protocol.",
